AWS 3-Tier Architecture Using Terraform !

Overview

This project demonstrates the design and implementation of a scalable, secure, and highly available 3-Tier Web Application Architecture on Amazon Web Services (AWS).
The architecture separates the application into three independent layers: Presentation Tier, Application Tier, and Database Tier. Each layer has specific responsibilities, improving security, scalability, maintainability, and performance.
The infrastructure is provisioned using **Terraform (Infrastructure as Code)**, making it easier to automate, manage, and reproduce cloud resources.

Architecture Components

1. Presentation Tier
- Application Load Balancer (ALB)
- Public Subnets
- Internet Gateway
- Handles incoming user requests and distributes traffic.

2. Application Tier
- Amazon EC2
- Auto Scaling Group
- Private Subnets
- Hosts application logic and processes user requests.

3. Database Tier
- Amazon RDS (MySQL/PostgreSQL)
- Private Database Subnets
- Stores and manages application data securely.

